<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The daily digest, at 08:00, from spec/search.yaml digest.schedule.

    cron: "0 8 * * *"      ->  StartCalendarInterval Hour 8, Minute 0
    timeout_seconds: 900   ->  DESK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, enforced by run-digest.sh

  Why the timeout is not a launchd key: there isn't one. ExitTimeOut is the
  grace period launchd allows between SIGTERM and SIGKILL when it is already
  trying to stop the job — it does not bound how long a running job may take.
  Nothing in launchd does. So the wall-clock limit is enforced by the wrapper
  script, and this file's only job is to hand it the number.

  Why any of this matters on this machine: with Power Nap, a scheduled job
  wakes inside a short window while the lid is shut. An unsupervised job with
  no timeout that hangs — a site that accepts the connection and never answers
  is enough — stays hung indefinitely, holds the run, and KeepAlive does not
  rescue it, because from launchd's point of view the job never exited.

  Note there is no send flag here. Telegram is off in the spec, and asking to
  send into a disabled channel is a hard error by design. Adding the flag is
  the second half of turning delivery on; see docs/session-7.md.

  This file is not installed by anything. Copying it into ~/Library/LaunchAgents
  is a deliberate act by a human, and so is removing it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.noamarazi.jobdesk</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk/deploy/launchd/run-digest.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>DESK_HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk</string>
        <!-- The explicit wall-clock ceiling. The wrapper refuses to run without it. -->
        <key>DESK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS</key>
        <string>900</string>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>8</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>

    <!-- Grace period after launchd asks the job to stop. Not a run-time limit. -->
    <key>ExitTimeOut</key>
    <integer>900</integer>

    <!-- A digest is not a daemon. It runs, it prints, it exits. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk/runs/digest.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk/runs/digest.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
